    "result": "I changed `solution.py` and the tests to address the mutation failure. The suite still passes (8 tests), but I haven't re-run the mutation gate, so I can't confirm the new score.\n\n- **Class checks:** I replaced the `_class_of` if-chain with a `_count_classes` helper that uses set intersections against `string.ascii_lowercase`, `string.ascii_uppercase` and `string.digits`. That removes most of the surviving mutants, which were boundary comparisons and return constants in the old chain. I added one test with characters at the class edges (`azAZ09azAZ09`).\n- **Type check:** The `or` → `and` mutant survived because `check_password(1, \"bob\", set())` still raised `TypeError` from `len(1)`. The type tests now use `match=\"must be str\"`, so only the explicit check satisfies them.",
